f 1079 #uuid "66bb6a07-ca7f-50c9-b79b-cace17e398e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186515109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c0a3ff9d-4c25-52f6-a5ce-1978a3171c0c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166599 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166599 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $y = 3\\sech{x}+\\coth{x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166599 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3817c58a-1176-5347-aa96-2846969cae32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166599 #edb/ref 1074 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFirst, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n( \\sech x )' = -\\sech x\\tanh x,\n\\quad \n( \\csch x )' = -\\csch x \\coth x,\n\\quad \n( \\coth x )' = -\\csch^2 x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results and the rules of differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =3(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)+(-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166600 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8350" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166600 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) =\\coth(5x - 2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166600 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b14f0558-456d-51a9-85ac-0b36158bc52e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166600 #edb/ref 1074 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf =\\coth{g}, \\qquad g = 5x - 2\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g}  = -\\csch^2{g},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x} = 5.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-{csch}^{2}⁡g\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-5{csch}^{2}⁡g \\\\  & =-5{csch}^{2}⁡(5x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166601 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8351" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166601 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = x^2\\coth{x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166601 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4baa8799-f8ce-521e-833b-8b66c747e701" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166601 #edb/ref 1074 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = x^2$ and $v(x) = \\coth{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot (-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =x(2\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166602 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8352" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166602 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\sech{x}}{4x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166602 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bec9b472-31ce-5892-8a17-c4aa3c33ef12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166602 #edb/ref 1074 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x) = \\sech{x}$ and $v(x) = 4x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot (4x)-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot {(4x)}^{′}}{{(4x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\cdot (4x)-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot 4}{16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+1)}{16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+1)}{4{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1039 "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186515591 #edb/ref 